      "id": 1,
      "text": "Gamerco was founded in 1920 as a company town by the Gallup American Coal Company.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gamerco%2C_New_Mexico"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In the 1960s the coal mines shut down, the power plant was decommissioned, and the railroad spur was removed.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gamerco%2C_New_Mexico"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "At its peak, about 500 coal miners and their families called Gamerco home.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gamerco%2C_New_Mexico"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The community sits in a basin that drains into Gamerco Wash, feeding the Puerco River and the Little Colorado watershed.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gamerco%2C_New_Mexico"
    },
    {
